{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>From the families of the tribe of Manasseh.</b> Since they perceived that the intent of the Most High El was that the inheritance should not pass around, even though He had given them permission to choose as they wished from the entire tribe, they chose the sons of their cousins from among all the families, because they were the closest." "<b>And their inheritance remained upon the tribe of their father's family.</b> And thus there was no transfer of inheritance at all, even from one family to another."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:41:41.676803671Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}